---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mastery Tutor Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for Mastery Tutor."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="page">
    <h1>Mastery Tutor Terms of Use</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective:</strong> September 4, 2026</p>

    <h2>Educational purpose</h2>
    <p>
      Mastery Tutor is an educational aid intended to support practice, explanation, self-assessment, and review.
      It does not guarantee mastery, academic outcomes, professional certification, or error-free subject-matter advice.
    </p>

    <h2>User responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Users remain responsible for verifying important technical, academic, professional, legal, medical, financial,
      or safety-critical information with appropriate authoritative sources or qualified professionals.
    </p>

    <h2>Service behavior</h2>
    <p>
      The v0.8.0 Tutor State Engine provides deterministic, read-only pedagogical recommendations. It does not modify
      external systems, create accounts, make purchases, or store a persistent learner profile.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The service may change, be interrupted, or become unavailable as OpenAI, Cloudflare, or the project itself evolves.
      Features may also vary by ChatGPT plan, region, workspace, model, and product surface.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not use the service to violate applicable law, platform policies, third-party rights, or access controls.
      Do not attempt to use the MCP endpoint to transmit secrets or unrelated sensitive data.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>These terms may be updated as the project or platform requirements change.</p>

    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>
      Questions and bug reports can be filed in the
      <a href="https://github.com/oozoofrog/mastery-tutor/issues">Mastery Tutor GitHub repository</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/mastery-tutor/">← Mastery Tutor</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto 4rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  h1, h2 { color: var(--dark-green); }
  h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
